// Title: HackTool - HiveSwarming Execution
// Sigma ID: a94aa3f9-97d3-46ac-ae02-94be9573acbe
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ammar Jokhadar (Thawd Security)
// Date: 2026-07-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects execution of HiveSwarming, a tool that converts Windows registry exports to registry
//   hive files and vice versa without requiring special privileges. This tool can be used to prepare
//   a modified user hive that is later staged as NTUSER.MAN for mandatory profile persistence.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of HiveSwarming by administrators, migration teams, or security professionals.
// References:
//   - https://deceptiq.com/blog/ntuser-man-registry-persistence
//   - https://github.com/stormshield/HiveSwarming
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/761f24ae2d4456a47936bec5b63984577fe9324f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_hiveswarming.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\HiveSwarming.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "HiveSwarming.exe"
